"""patch_prereg_addendum11_1030.py (2026-10-30): appends Addendum 11 (the rebuild procedure for event_daily_range_coverage, the last flag of G7) to results/PREREG_g7_proven_rerun_2026-10-29.md.
The registration must be exactly the version after Addendum 10a (sha256 4ac3f8d6...) and the placeholder must occur exactly once, or nothing is changed.
No registered prediction is edited: the text before PRED-TABLE-END is compared before and after.
Usage: python3 scripts/audit/patch_prereg_addendum11_1030.py [results/PREREG_g7_proven_rerun_2026-10-29.md]"""
import hashlib, sys
def sha(s): return hashlib.sha256((s if s.endswith("\n") else s + "\n").encode("utf-8")).hexdigest()
p = sys.argv[1] if len(sys.argv) > 1 else "results/PREREG_g7_proven_rerun_2026-10-29.md"
T = open(p, encoding="utf-8").read()
assert sha(T) == "4ac3f8d6ecca0b15736bbb8d105fc921b1fc0a49115c15ce8a047d15e598d73b", "the registration is not the version after Addendum 10a; nothing changed"
old = "(further dated addenda go here: the remaining procedures)"
assert T.count(old) == 1, "placeholder not found exactly once; nothing changed"
new = """### Addendum 11 (2026-10-30, before the build): event_daily_range_coverage, the last flag; a rebuild of its two day-lists and a directly computed readout

**Correction to this registration.** The inventory row of this flag says the procedure was not located. That was wrong: the whole procedure is in the session of 2026-10-16 16:27 and its objects exist in the database. This addendum replaces that row.

**What the flag measures.** For events of the ordinary types (not capital_raise, not bundled summary events, not spin-off or separation titles), the day 0 and day +1 stock-days are flagged; the control is the same stocks' days +25 to +39 of the same events with flagged days removed. Coverage is the share of days whose raw close-to-close move is below 1.19 times the stock's own 64-day volatility estimate (bin <= 118 of the histogram, k_ref 1.18 chosen so that ordinary days of 2004-2018 cover 80 percent). The shortfall is the control coverage minus the flagged coverage, in points. The ledger row (status proven, tested 2026-10-16, multiplier 1.25) carries a three-part rule: (1) flagged-day coverage at least 5 points below ordinary days in both eras; (2) a multiplier fitted on one era brings the other within plus or minus 3 points; (3) the matched control still shows at least 5 points. The REGISTERED rows test part (3) only: p21 and p22 (the shortfall versus control, 2004-2018 and 2019-2026, registered 6.8 with interval 6.0 to 7.6 and 9.3 with 8.3 to 10.3) and p23 (still passes: 0.97), with the rule of this registration: 5 points or more in both eras.

**The stored result, recomputed on 2026-10-30 from the stored z_hist** (the control readout recovered from the 2026-10-16 session, run before this addendum): flagged day 0 or +1 0.7388 (n 22,410) and 0.7230 (n 10,827); control 0.8061 (n 140,533) and 0.8152 (n 71,031); ordinary days 0.8026 (n 1,540,356) and 0.8085 (n 899,115); so the shortfalls versus control are 6.73 and 9.22 points; the day +1 only group, from the 2026-10-16 print, 0.7547 (n 10,854) and 0.7325 (n 5,268). The ledger's evidence rows hold 0.0638 and 0.0673 (versus control) with SE 0.0029 and 0.0031 for 2004-2018 and 0.0855 and 0.0922 with SE 0.0043 and 0.0045 for 2019-2026 (naive SEs). The stored objects: flag_days 51,239 rows (34,508 with day 0 or +1; 2003-12-31 to 2026-08-03), ctrl_days 218,904 rows (last day 2026-07-27), z_hist 31,425 raw, 29,590 abn and 8,810 rawc rows, spy_cal 8,250 rows (last day 2026-10-13); no day is in both lists.

**What is rebuilt and what is not.** The live definitions of build_z_hist and build_z_ctrl were read from the database on 2026-10-30 and equal the 2026-10-16 text (whitespace-insensitive comparison, done programmatically). The two statements that built flag_days and ctrl_days, and the DELETE that removed the overlap, were recovered from that transcript; the rebuild files copy them clause for clause (checked programmatically after renaming), and no later session modified those tables (all transcripts searched). The rebuild is into NEW tables: ARM 0 (flag_days_g7_arm0, ctrl_days_g7_arm0) is the original procedure on today's inputs; ARM 1 (flag_days_g7_arm1, ctrl_days_g7_arm1) is the same with events that have an exclude row in event_exclusions left out of both lists. The readout is computed DIRECTLY from market_prices and vol_estimators for the days of each list (the return is the close over the previous close within the same window as the original build, v64 above 0, days from 2004-01-01 to 2026-07-31), instead of through the histogram and its twelve year-blocks per arm. Parts (1) and (2) of the ledger rule need the unflagged histogram and the full bin range and are NOT rebuilt: they stand as in the ledger (shortfall versus ordinary days 0.0638 and 0.0855 in the evidence rows; held-out multipliers 1.195 and 1.288), read from the stored tables only.

**The method check, fixed now (QUERY M).** The direct readout is first run on the STORED tables flag_days and ctrl_days. It must reproduce six cells exactly in n and to four decimals in coverage: flagged day 0 or +1 (22,410 and 0.7388; 10,827 and 0.7230), day +1 only (10,854 and 0.7547; 5,268 and 0.7325) and control (140,533 and 0.8061; 71,031 and 0.8152). If any cell differs, the direct readout is not used for ARM 0 or ARM 1, nothing of ARM 0 or ARM 1 is read, and the histogram route is registered in a new addendum.

**The build and the reading, fixed now.** (1) scripts/sql/g7_range_build_arm0_2026-10-30.sql and the arm1 file create the new tables. (2) scripts/sql/g7_range_compare_2026-10-30.sql holds QUERY M, QUERY D (distinct keys, rows only in one table, rows whose flags differ, ARM 0 against ARM 1) and the readouts QUERY 0 (ARM 0) and QUERY 1 (ARM 1); they are run in the order M, D, 0, 1. (3) The shortfall of an arm and an era is 100 times the control coverage minus the flagged day 0 or +1 coverage. The registered p21 is the ARM 1 shortfall of 2004-2018 and p22 that of 2019-2026; p23 is true if both are 5.0 points or more. ARM 0 and the stored values are reported beside them; the day +1 only shortfall is reported as descriptive. The SE is naive, sqrt(p(1-p)/n) added over the two groups, as in the ledger; days of the same events and weeks cluster, so a clustered SE would be larger and is not computed here.

**Tripwires.** (1) QUERY M reproduces the six cells (above). (2) In QUERY D the row count of each day-list equals its distinct-key count (no repeated keys; the lesson of the premium rebuild). (3) ARM 1's flag list is contained in ARM 0's: flag_arm1 - flag_arm0 + flag_in_arm0_not_arm1 must be 0. (4) The stored tables are not modified: QUERY M re-reads them. (5) If ARM 0 differs from the stored lists, the difference is measured and attributed in QUERY D before the readouts of ARM 0 or ARM 1 are read.

**Stated in advance.** (a) ARM 0 may differ from the stored lists for three known reasons: the view event_component_dates (candidate_review_log was touched on 2026-10-29), the date corrections of 2026-10-29 (a corrected date moves up to three flagged days and fifteen control days of that event), and events added since 2026-10-16 with a date before 2026-08-01. (b) ARM 1 is expected to be almost identical to ARM 0, and this is a judgment from the excluded rows seen in the premium rebuild, not a measurement: an excluded event with a price step touches only the flagged days that fall on the step (the Keurig Dr Pepper step of 2018-07-10 is day +1 of the two events of 2018-07-09, one stock-day; the KLA-Tencor step is four days after its event), and an excluded event with no price history has day-list rows but no price rows, so it does not enter the readout. QUERY D counts the flag rows ARM 1 removes but not how many of them have prices; the n of the readouts shows it. (c) The margin to the 5-point line is 1.7 points in 2004-2018 (about 5.5 naive SEs) and 4.2 points in 2019-2026 (about 9 naive SEs). (d) The frozen forward test of the ledger (multiplier 1.25, events after 2026-07-31) is NOT touched; as registered above, the frozen forward tests are evaluated once after 2027-01-05. (e) Sealed versus non-sealed is not reported (no company-set split). (f) The new tables are additive, nothing existing is modified, and they are listed for deletion after 2026-11-28 (flag_days_g7_arm0, flag_days_g7_arm1, ctrl_days_g7_arm0, ctrl_days_g7_arm1). Nothing here re-scores or edits a prediction.

(further dated addenda go here: the remaining procedures)"""
head_before = T[:T.index("PRED-TABLE-END")]
R = T.replace(old, new)
assert R[:R.index("PRED-TABLE-END")] == head_before, "a registered prediction would change; nothing written"
open(p, "w", encoding="utf-8").write(R)
R2 = open(p, encoding="utf-8").read(); print("ok   Addendum 11 appended"); print("PREREG sha256", sha(R2), "|", R2.count("\n"), "lines")
